    {
      "id": "b9622b577838dc9910ce212ef15f608846d5f98f649a309ede160783492a399c",
      "text": "AI Coding Dictionary",
      "hash": "4def77f9388809f53620144510fcc4b6f08662617bcc06a15abc618242e6544c"
    },
    {
      "id": "af7fe00d547cea738adf55ed636c790e23c4883a51e4b917b5659872cb375cb6",
      "text": "Topics",
      "hash": "e22820fcf5cd90e3fdd99a7569e0ee2f30eb7ebadfb2fe4d159b30c166ff81b7"
    },
    {
      "id": "63d2d40d3af71c43f5925ee508f9165ba9a955fcd21f1931e94e9bfe18e9630b",
      "text": "The Model",
      "hash": "1954409637324f1c3f2cab102211fd161a6cd1c270252fc2e1297a69ab9a446b"
    },
    {
      "id": "79113a6cb189d977355e089e94fb967ae98e5cfa6fdbfb8b00325cb7aa3aed0a",
      "text": "Non-determinism",
      "hash": "29528d719817ee2e8c9f3bb920e7820ebe1ff4bc1afc1e91f25ef655e25d4b01"
    },
    {
      "id": "fede9d890436b8c8f58e7cbb1b2d083af60e2a594b94ed98e2972564a12d92fd",
      "text": "The same input can produce different output. A property of how models generate text and how providers serve requests.",
      "hash": "f1700615d5d5a3a32b8dfecf068a5038783adef2707c4bc73bf149b00b2987ba"
    },
    {
      "id": "c3a446a142209bdb873250bc9958c629598a854fa8a33838534809c33d48d1a9",
      "text": "Matt Pocock",
      "hash": "2fe2c13509fbd45ec2578a74ef8efda313caad4f19533a102ca7d666ed60881d"
    },
    {
      "id": "47eadd06d6ea511d593cc39b9ac56d479725d78e0e28be44b6bca62fd13c032e",
      "text": "Copy page",
      "hash": "4104018941ae3ab016c117887a91b4f933f28e36c587b8983373fe9377ce34d7"
    },
    {
      "id": "41628ef58bd682746f2dd961ca99e47386a2ff9060aaa76f80a591de6be70e1c",
      "text": "The same input can produce different output. Run a",
      "hash": "d8738982dee9ff8ae2cca23a64616632916fa05aa12bb21de31f71d9ac643c0d"
    },
    {
      "id": "d7044138b6ad025c1556ac8b90412cfe9c538a281b698fb7dcda5d30906602d3",
      "text": "twice with identical",
      "hash": "b00470afab124722caa20766c82c85eac86568f810663ad51cf6092ce96f7591"
    },
    {
      "id": "3a0ca33c7967009f11e7d254da0fe57e4bead8d8d83eb38dbff4952f396640e4",
      "text": "and you may get two different answers — sometimes a word, sometimes a completely different approach. Nothing in your code has to change for this to happen.",
      "hash": "822d5cf253b407bf83f9e71059d0ba99906c9de4aa53267671a7e90a19631edc"
    },
    {
      "id": "dc6d2b1d9801848fbc5b0a3bc4679e93a207a19ac4dc3d12c1f79767d2ab65c1",
      "text": "It's a property of how models generate text, and how",
      "hash": "e6a9177fe2683bf5bfec49de5695a7163018000cb893ef533c95f7f78601c942"
    },
    {
      "id": "6c290247b7e92ce3833845088c4c68499911490616126d93a1af0d3bff70cf63",
      "text": "model providers",
      "hash": "7548fb2cfbf65b3b06af90570f4b0f0cd1fe9d1b679d4f495b31bd5c08cfdbbd"
    },
    {
      "id": "f63dcae39e30411c00ea2ba41db55fbe8c40409443725d8b5d44796bd5d4c22c",
      "text": ". During",
      "hash": "49c7a70400c24ee41dd9cf1a66b4412a89bba2443a67a6c32f78aa7fdf35dc2c"
    },
    {
      "id": "6b37fd6ac9ba4c0312bfc5aebe579787f88f95011090f563a7525f28dc5bb411",
      "text": ", the model produces a probability distribution over possible next",
      "hash": "9ca4d63bbc7b76fc35b530a15a17fe2f8cc90cf75f3dca4b64be06974358e9be"
    },
    {
      "id": "901798e9dcc4c595594a8f6f53ef0225cca74d82226579cf9aaa6464de98d6a4",
      "text": "and one is sampled from it — usually with some randomness on purpose, since always picking the most likely token produces repetitive, lower-quality text. One differently-sampled token early in a response changes every token after it, which is how a single different word becomes a completely different approach. Provider-side serving adds more variation on top: requests are batched together on shared hardware, and tiny floating-point differences between batches can tip a close call between two tokens. There's no setting you can flip to make it all go away.",
      "hash": "d747ca19a3b93629a0eb2de55217a4f40755869a8edb366515aebd92a9fc8543"
    },
    {
      "id": "5c62edc66f511117905f3901ebd5103c1bd2775ef29e757567d8a8cc51bea776",
      "text": "Expect a spread of results from an",
      "hash": "bf6666523fb353ff05d1cb1e7513b3a32a75f80ceaafafaf8c6872fc23be9796"
    },
    {
      "id": "cfaca3e0057d434ffb600f815bc5260825957b9fe9f9bfc684b514bd2227f065",
      "text": "on the same task. Most responses fall within a reasonable bell curve of quality — that's why the non-determinism is tolerable at all — but the tails are real: some days the model will feel sharp; some days it'll feel like it's lost the plot. Same task, different rolls of the dice. This has two practical consequences. Retrying is a legitimate strategy: a failed attempt is one draw from the distribution, and a fresh attempt at the same task may simply land better. And verification matters more than it would with deterministic tools — you can't test an agent's behaviour once and rely on it repeating, so",
      "hash": "511cd1eb92e686da5f2caffd0bf490669f759f15bbda3061ab89f75b46c9c074"
    },
    {
      "id": "23bec92b199d153dc3747095baf2627b9da5f56aa666474bf8136206c83290fc",
      "text": "automated checks",
      "hash": "f748d6acc6e10f9e80812a46b239b1d2f3f145075600d299b6e40632fb06622b"
    },
    {
      "id": "f0a40c52984f7b0b52de014670675ff06e4daf7484d24cf9d074deaec08db9b3",
      "text": "have to catch the bad draws.",
      "hash": "b6b61dce81ee03bbb6c2b0487fd7171115526165db5e968605b9f7b175a1e9ca"
    },
    {
      "id": "b35636e31f4e6c0294901a8ae334bbaaacec1ede76c0095846ddff061e783383",
      "text": "Be careful not to over-narrativize this. Humans are pattern-matching machines, and a string of bad runs can feel like proof that \"the model got worse this week.\" Usually it's just the distribution.",
      "hash": "2cd73f32e6fd6c2cff365fd8b33b0b43bf15c47c3d79d606a10798624c93cb68"
    },
    {
      "id": "adaa00293ba9a60b8c4d34528f9008d06019f5635ae8e8caea52a78ded277ed2",
      "text": "Usage:",
      "hash": "2bad3eeaf33caffe3bc9b482b4934ed19eb4ec3614c12373e1a5c5f8948217da"
    },
    {
      "id": "47fd45c36b0cf5da0dfa2fa1eee6ada732fc5d039ff6d0a56a424314bf941c4a",
      "text": "\"Claude has been awful today. Did they ship a worse version?\"",
      "hash": "04c1c9449fe83f199725679c5cca7971103ae3f455cc37caedafa3f0c688b384"
    },
    {
      "id": "63098b926d2cef885625f4a3c6eebf030b43fe6ab51b7a938b5ac7e5146a58e5",
      "text": "\"Probably not — model output is non-deterministic. You're going to have good days and bad days on the same task. Try again tomorrow before you go looking for a cause.\"",
      "hash": "c78de6cee7095be8a96bec930e5c24d4f55da05216b3a627574a5f2c8c7f7658"
    },
    {
      "id": "7657137d09ed75abed732ee784599d2d1a2a03dd0e66a1fc14fb11d6b9dd50fc",
      "text": "Previous term",
      "hash": "735604aff9e8f2192b83df4905cfc8e395613e0ce05f8ca85a1d2d1d44fd59f3"
    },
    {
      "id": "23138a5c12873279c032af8fa8b0345033a53a3655cec38e7f7898735f111077",
      "text": "Next-token prediction",
      "hash": "db2e13aa671f566f6c582c8ff074e0b702a81659695c239d0634c86b0e328583"
    },
    {
      "id": "12462f91c1835e5c66c8a7dd302a94341ef0e79663b3a98bf1f2c2fb11bfe71c",
      "text": "Next term",
      "hash": "5219c7ebdc0e098aa6db6f09e405c1b17ab75f1082862906a872e10a16818f9e"
    },
    {
      "id": "eb3a5112b47a5098fa530257488fb6e6d69622ac4f2a929d921f1b35f7fe447d",
      "text": "Model provider",
      "hash": "ea70384c465d5c89fb7cdd19647c540c4025a1c17532dcb8b987d7b753cf8596"
    },
    {
      "id": "1aafc48af92159482cbaf6dbffc131d01d572672fd6f2e4f4baad4f4f19863dd",
      "text": "Want more than vocabulary?",
      "hash": "5d5500a083006a1606e84a03c018904d01364631c6baea4c7a3f8f3f62bf94dc"
